[01:43.93] Houses iced in whitewash guard a pale shore-line
[01:54.08] Cornered by the cactus and the pine
[02:03.74] Here I wander where sweet sage and strange herbs grow
[02:13.19] Down a crumpled sun-baked stony road
[02:23.12] Dusty wheels leaning rusting in the sun
[02:33.14] Snuff brown walls where Spanish lizards run
[02:43.48] Here I'm shadowed by a dragon fig tree's fan
[02:53.35] Ringed by ants and musing over man
[03:02.90] 
[03:22.93] I'll unwind my old strings while the sun shine down
[03:31.43] Won't climb any high thing while the sun shine
[03:39.78] Formentera Lady, sing your song for me
[03:47.85] Formentera Lady, sun lover
[03:57.61] 
[04:02.45] Lamplight glows on old guitars the travellers strum
[04:11.77] Incense children dance to an Indian drum
[04:20.22] Here Odysseus charmed for dark Circe fell
[04:29.02] Still her perfume lingers, still her spell
[04:38.67] 
[04:42.11] Time's grey hand won't catch me while the stars shine down
[04:50.34] Untie and unlatch me while the stars shine
[04:58.66] Formentera Lady, dance your dance for me
[05:06.82] Formentera Lady, dark lover...
[05:15.02] 